                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "27b722a5-3299-3bed-8457-a310e0447954",
                        "entry_id": "add55bab-12bc-3d2f-a3c4-94fbad0b3fd0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Forme de conflit, humain ou animal, où un groupe d’individus cherche à obtenir une position dominante mais en reconnaissant l’existence de l’autre. Il se distingue donc de l’antagonisme par sa volonté de ne pas exclure l’adversaire."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bdbce656-4aca-4d6f-b2a9-bfcec679b814",
                                "sense_id": "27b722a5-3299-3bed-8457-a310e0447954",
                                "text": "Dans ce cadre, il est clair que tout fond religieux a disparu: l’énigme représente toujours un danger extrême, mais son terrain est seulement un agonisme humain."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "71ea1b98-582f-4f1e-b73a-49e2a136ebfe",
                                "sense_id": "27b722a5-3299-3bed-8457-a310e0447954",
                                "text": "Paradoxalement, la forme associative de la démocratie, caractéristique de l’obsession consensuelle du social-libéralisme, alimente l’antagonisme quand, au contraire, le conflit entre la droite et la gauche qu’Emmanuel Macron a voulu dépasser en affaiblissant ses adversaires – de droite comme de gauche – nourrissait vertueusement ce qui fait l’essence de la démocratie : l’agonisme."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "14aff8b1-06e4-4d32-8750-63f41f20a000",
                        "source_entry_id": "add55bab-12bc-3d2f-a3c4-94fbad0b3fd0",
                        "source_sense_id": "27b722a5-3299-3bed-8457-a310e0447954",
                        "target_lang_word": "agonism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "agonism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1eec9464-d065-3a89-ba39-59aea2e38d3e",
                                        "entry_id": "f9fe0f8b-5dc2-3170-b2ad-89831dd4e858",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Competitive struggle (especially political)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "00c784b3-7c43-4ead-8ac3-81e556047a6a",
                                                "sense_id": "1eec9464-d065-3a89-ba39-59aea2e38d3e",
                                                "text": "The internal competition between tendencies or natures that Machiavelli recognizes in individuals and groups and that Nietzsche sees as multiple drives is a form of “agonism.” Agonism is the idea that conflict and struggle are the natural basis of life and that this is replicated in social, political, and cultural life."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d0b21f4-9505-44a9-a439-c79bf511520e",
                                                "sense_id": "1eec9464-d065-3a89-ba39-59aea2e38d3e",
                                                "text": "This is where the great replacement comes in. As mendacious and deranged as it is, it provides a structural explanation for various aspects of the polycrisis, and comes with in-built agonism for politicians to exploit."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "607d164d-42b2-3720-a597-dfef0ed8838b",
                                        "entry_id": "f9fe0f8b-5dc2-3170-b2ad-89831dd4e858",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The relationship between an agonist and a receptor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
